{
  "_doc": "Enemy rows. tier feeds progression; gen names the creature table used by the view. attacks: what it can swing. Each weapon (arms: scythe | axe | spear | club; Sim.ARMS gives each Trolloc one by id) has its own two, the first its favourite: a scythe-sword sweeps wide and chops, an axe chops hard and sweeps, a spear thrusts from further off and shoves with the haft, a club smashes down and shoves. Which one is chosen by what is in front of it (Sim._pick_blow): never a high sweep at someone ducking, the wide one when two stand in it, the long one from further off, the heavy one at someone who keeps parrying, and seldom the same twice. on: what the blow does to the one it lands on unguarded (stagger = s reeling, push = thrown back m/s). kind names the motion; height high can be ducked, over (a chop coming down) cannot; arc is the half-angle it covers, fixed when the swing starts, so stepping out of it makes it miss; time, dmg and reach multiply the row's own numbers. ranged: an archer (range it will shoot from, keep = the distance it likes, time between arrows, dmg, arrow speed and gravity). evades: share of blows and weaves a Myrddraal is simply not there for, unless staggered or bound. steady: cannot be knocked down. links: Trollocs that arrive in the same wave die when it dies. fester: its wounds go on hurting (secs, dps) until Healed. stalk: the distance a Myrddraal circles at between attacks. lunge: from between min and max metres it crouches (wind s, the tell), then goes dist metres at speed along the line it chose; dmg multiplies its damage; open = s it is helpless if it misses. shadow: it vanishes (first use after `first` s, then every `every` s), is gone for `gone` s and untouchable, and comes out `dist` metres behind its victim, striking `appear` s later. Darkhound: pounce is a lunge without the stalking (on = what the hit does to you); regen: hp per s it mends once left alone for `after` s; steel: share of weapon damage that counts (weaves count in full). Draghkar: song: it flies (untouchable) at `fly` m/s to 0.65 x range, lands, sings for `hold` s (hurt it, or break its line of sight, and the song fails), then its victim walks to it at `pull` m/s for up to `last` s unable to act, and at touch it drains `drain` of their health per s for `kiss` s. Dreadlord: channels (can be Shielded); ranged with weapon dark_fire bursts in `blast` m and is gathered for `wind` s first; strike: lightning on a marked circle (radius) `wind` s after it is marked, every `every` s.",
